This section presents one implementation of the conceptual architecture presented in last section. After many refactorings, a framework called SABIA (Speech-Act-Based Intelligent Agents Framework) has been developed and CognIA (Cognitive Investment Advisor) application has been developed as an instantiation of SABIA framework. We present then the accuracy and some automated tests of this implementation.

Speech-Act-based Intelligent Agents Framework

SABIA was developed on top of Akka middleware. Akka is a toolkit and runtime that implements the Actor Model on the JVM. Akka's features, like concurrency, distributed computing, resilience, and message-passing were inspired by Erlang's actor model BIBREF44 BIBREF45 . The actor model is a mathematical model of concurrent computation that treats "actors" as the universal primitives of concurrent computation. In response to a message that it receives, an actor can: make local decisions, create more actors, send more messages, and determine how to respond to the next received message. Actors

